  "metadata": {
    "title": "Observational data and model output to \"SNOWstorm (v1.0) - a deep-learning based model for near-surface winds and drifting snow in mountain environments\"",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.18670232",
    "publication_date": "2026-02-17",
    "description": "<p><strong>Observational data:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p>Raw data from three automated weather stations (AWS) at Hintereisferner glacier, Austria,&nbsp; used in the validation of the case studie in \"SNOWstorm (v1.0) - a deep-learning based model for near-surface winds and drifting snow in mountain environments\", under revision in Geoscientific&nbsp; Model Development ( https://doi.org/10.5194/egusphere-2025-5608);</p>\n<p>also described in&nbsp; \"A novel framework to investigate wind-driven snow redistribution over an Alpine glacier: combination of high-resolution terrestrial laser scans and large-eddy simulations\", https://doi.org/10.5194/tc-18-849-2024.</p>\n<p>2021_AWS_HEF.csv: data from temporary AWS on the glacier</p>\n<p>data_sth_202102.csv: data from station Hintereis</p>\n<p>202101-03_ImHinterenEis_FRecDR_calc_TKE.csv: data from station Im Hinteren Eis.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Model output:</strong></p>\n<p>ts_snowstorm_obs_20210208.nc: Model output of SNOWstorm for case study: time series of surface-level wind extracted at grid points of AWS locations&nbsp;</p>\n<p>ds_snow_acc*.nc: accumulated drifting snow fields for the case study experiments&nbsp;</p>\n<p>ds_S_*.nc: SNOWstorm output fields at example time step used in the manuscript for experiments with different input settings&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
